course: dictionary
lesson: 1580
title: Chase in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Chase has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «Scientists found rats make high chirps when tickled, and chase the tickling hand for more» means the rats move after the hand, wanting more. Chase here means to run or move after something.
explain: «Snake charmers' cobras do not dance to music, mambas do not chase horses» is a sentence that corrects a myth. The clue is that a snake would not hunt a horse. Chase means to run after something to catch it. Try the swap: put "run after" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Chase also works in phrases. To chase away means to make someone go away. To cut to the chase means to get to the main point. Read the whole phrase, because the meaning of chase changes with the words beside it.
fact: To chase means to run after someone or something to catch it.
fact: A chase is the act of running after someone, as in a police chase or a cat-and-mouse chase in a story.
fact: To chase a dream means to try hard to get it.
fact: In nature, predators chase prey: a cheetah chases a gazelle.
fact: «Old Man Kangaroo is chased» is a story about being chased, so chase can be used in tales as well as in real life.
exercise: «Real otters do not chase May-flies, and real toads walk slowly to their ponds.» What does chase mean here? | To sleep under a log | *To run after something to catch it | To wash clean | To sing loudly
exercise: Mum says, «Chase away those flies from the kitchen.» What does chase away mean? | *To make them go away by running at them | To feed them crumbs | To count them slowly | To invite them in for tea
exercise: In «The chase ended at the river», what kind of word is chase? | An adjective that describes the river | A place by the river | *A noun: the act of running after someone | A verb that means to swim
test: What does chase mean in «rats chase the tickling hand for more»? | To sing softly | To lie still and wait | To hide under the bed | *To run after, wanting more
test: «Cut to the chase» means | Run very fast in a race | Start a long story from the beginning | *Get to the main point | Cut a piece of cake into small slices
exam: Which meaning fits «A cheetah chases a gazelle across the plain»? | Gives it a bath in the river | *Runs after it to catch it | Waves goodbye as it leaves | Sleeps in the shade while the gazelle grazes
